## Error Handling Rules

```
INSTRUCTION TO AI:
- When user pastes an error message, identify the error type first
- Never ask user to re-do the entire setup for a single error
- Always isolate which step failed and fix only that step
- Common error → fix mapping below:
```

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `No such file or directory: requirements.txt` | Wrong directory or clone failed | `cd D:\ComfyUI` then check files exist |
| `CUDA out of memory` | Missing `--lowvram` flag | Add `--lowvram` to launch command |
| `No module named torch` | venv not activated | Run activate command first |
| `cuda.is_available() = False` | Driver issue or wrong PyTorch | Update NVIDIA driver |
| `git not recognized` | Git not installed | Redo Step 2 |
| `py -3.10 not found` | Python 3.10 not installed | Redo Step 1 |

